// Build 1674: the program size counts the AVR interrupt vector table's unused words.
// Each vector has a 2-word slot; a 1-word reti or rjmp leaves a word the program cannot use. Before 1674
// those words were not counted (26 on the ATmega328P), so "Program Memory" was short and the size check
// could pass a program that did not fit. Expected: Program Memory = Code Segment + 1024 (ReserveHighProg).
#Chip mega328p, 16
#option ReserveHighProg OPTIBOOT
On Interrupt Timer1Overflow Call TimerTick
Do
Loop

Sub TimerTick
    PortB = 1
End Sub
